      },
      "problem": "The stop repeatedly requires luck rather than reasoned picks. Cards 2 and 3 ask for the temple's treatment and Jerusalem's condition when card 1 has supplied only the invasion. Cards 8 and 9 ask about God's anger and burning jealousy when card 7 supplies only \"How long, O LORD?\" Card 6 likewise gives no setup for the neighbors' reaction. These are too many discovery questions for one stop, leaving half or more of its choices uninformed.",
      "rule": {
        "link": "prep-walkthrough.md#an-informed-guess-never-luck",
        "text": "The check: could a thoughtful baker who has only seen the earlier cards make a reasoned pick? If the only way to get it right is luck, give the story card more context or ask a different question. A few of those are okay, as long as most choice cards are informed guesses."
      },
